  "services": {
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Life Moves Pretty Fast: The John Hughes Mixtapes is a 2022 compilation album released by Demon Records and Hughes Music, featuring a curated selection of music from the iconic films of director John Hughes. Spanning genres such as Electronic, Rock, and Funk/Soul, the album showcases the eclectic soundtrack choices that defined Hughes’ movies from 1983 to 1989. The tracklist includes influential new wave, synth pop, and alternative rock acts like The Thompson Twins, Spandau Ballet, Yello, and Silicon Teens, reflecting the era’s vibrant musical landscape and Hughes’ keen ear for emerging sounds.\n\nAs a retrospective collection, the album stands as a definitive musical companion to Hughes’ filmography, highlighting how music was integral to the emotional and cultural impact of his work. Curated by Hughes’ longtime music supervisor Tarquin Gotch, the set gathers both well-known hits and deeper cuts, offering fans and new listeners a comprehensive overview of the soundtracks that helped shape the teen movie genre. The compilation received positive critical attention for its thoughtful curation and historical significance, praised for capturing the spirit of the 1980s and the unique synergy between Hughes’ films and their music.",
      "generated_at": "2025-11-27T11:50:18.843747",
